  <!--
    ProjectReferences to the already-migrated SDK-style upstream projects (Requirement 2.4).
    All four had reached their clean-compile gate before this task started: Nop.Core (2.5),
    Nop.Data (3.3), Nop.Services (4.3) and Nop.Web.Framework (6.6).

    The legacy <Project>{GUID}</Project> / <Name>...</Name> metadata children are dropped -
    the SDK resolves references by path:
      {6BDA8332-939F-45B7-A25E-7A797260AE59} Nop.Core
      {ccd7f2c9-6a2c-4cf0-8e89-076b8fc0f144} Nop.Data
      {210541AD-F659-47DA-8763-16F36C5CD2F4} Nop.Services
      {75FD4163-333C-4DD5-854D-2EF294E45D94} Nop.Web.Framework

    NO reference to Nop.Web is added, and none was removed: the legacy project file had
    exactly these four. Nop.Web and Nop.Admin are siblings over Nop.Web.Framework
    (design section 6), and adding an edge in either direction would be a design change,
    not a migration. If task 8.2 decides the Nop.Web host must load this assembly, that
    is a hosting/discovery decision for 8.2 to make and document.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\..\Libraries\Nop.Core\Nop.Core.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\..\Libraries\Nop.Data\Nop.Data.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\..\Libraries\Nop.Services\Nop.Services.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Nop.Web.Framework\Nop.Web.Framework.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    ===================================================================================
    PUBLISH SHAPING - TASK 8.1, RUNTIME DEFERRAL 7.4-2. SECURITY RELEVANT.
    ===================================================================================
    3.90 shaped its publish output from Nop.Web.csproj, whose ExcludeFilesFromDeployment
    list included TWO entries that belong to THIS tree:

        Administration\bin\**
        Administration\db_backups\*.bak     <- DATABASE BACKUPS

    Task 7.4 could not re-express either of them, because Administration\** is in
    Nop.Web.csproj's DefaultItemExcludes, so nothing under this directory is an item of
    that project. It recorded the gap as deferral 7.4-2 and assigned it here.

    Administration\bin\** needs no entry - the SDK never publishes intermediate output,
    and the flat 3.90 ..\bin\ OutputPath is gone.

    db_backups is the security-relevant one and is handled below.

    Both directions are needed, for the same reason task 7.4 discovered on the storefront
    side (runtime-deferrals.md section 31.4): the legacy project used ~1200 explicit
    <Content Include=.../> entries to copy Content\ and Scripts\ into the output, but the
    SDK classifies .js/.css/.png/.gif/.woff/.map/.svg/.eot/.ttf/.otf/.swf as `None`, and
    `None` items default to CopyToPublishDirectory=Never. WITHOUT the first ItemGroup
    below a published Nop.Admin would have NO admin CSS, NO admin JavaScript, NO AdminLTE
    or bootstrap assets, NO TinyMCE and NO Roxy Fileman - i.e. an entirely unstyled,
    non-functional admin UI. That is a functional regression, not untidiness, and it is
    not something deferral 7.4-2 called out.

    `Update` is used rather than `Include` throughout: every one of these files is ALREADY
    an item from implicit globbing. `Include` would produce duplicates and fail the build
    with NETSDK1022; `Update` only changes metadata, and no-ops harmlessly for a path that
    does not exist.

    RESOLVED BY TASK 8.5 - the SERVING half of deferral 7.4-2. 8.5 widened
    Nop.Web\Infrastructure\NopStaticFileProvider.cs's allow-list with
    Administration/Content/** and Administration/Scripts/**, rather than relocating the
    trees under wwwroot. Relocation was rejected on measured grounds: TWO admin call sites
    read these directories as CONTENT-ROOT-RELATIVE PHYSICAL PATHS, not URLs -
    RoxyFilemanController's confFile (~/Administration/Content/Roxy_Fileman/conf.json) and
    TinyMceHelper.GetTinyMceLanguage()'s probe of
    ~/Administration/Content/tinymce/langs/{culture}.js, the second of which fails SILENTLY
    by falling back to English. See the AllowedAdministrationRoots remarks in that file.
    8.5 also had to change the publish paths here - see the Link note below.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      (a) Runtime assets that MUST reach the publish output.

      Content\  - the admin stylesheets and images (adminLTE, bootstrap, kendo, TinyMCE,
                  Roxy Fileman, fonts) plus Content\Roxy_Fileman\conf.json, which
                  RoxyFilemanController READS at runtime (Configuration()/GetSetting()).
      Scripts\  - the admin JavaScript (kendo, fineuploader, tagEditor, typeahead, ...).
      db_backups\ - for the placeholder ONLY; the .bak files are withheld immediately
                  below. This entry is NOT redundant and it is NOT cosmetic - see the
                  measured defect note in the withheld block.

      =================================================================================
      TASK 8.5 - THE `Link` METADATA IS LOAD-BEARING. DO NOT REMOVE IT.
      =================================================================================
      Without it these items publish to the publish root as Content\..., Scripts\... and
      db_backups\..., which is WRONG for two independent, measured reasons.

      (1) IT DOES NOT MATCH THE URL. Every admin view requests these assets as
          ~/Administration/Content/... and ~/Administration/Scripts/... (task 8.4 audited
          all 81 such references and fixed two casing defects in _AdminLayout.cshtml).
          Nop.Web's NopStaticFileProvider resolves a request subpath against the HOST's
          CONTENT ROOT - which is the project directory under `dotnet run` and the PUBLISH
          DIRECTORY in a deployment. So a published app must have the assets at
          Administration/Content/** and Administration/Scripts/**, or task 8.5's widened
          allow-list matches the URL and then finds nothing on disk: a 404 in the published
          app only, with the development build working perfectly.

      (2) IT COLLIDES WITH Nop.Web's OWN ASSET TREES. Deferral 8.2-2's suggested remedy is
          to "publish both projects into one directory", and MEASURED against the flat
          layout that silently overwrites files. Nop.Web has its own Content\ and Scripts\
          at the publish root, and the overlap is not hypothetical:
            Content\   : ionicons, jquery-ui-themes                       (2 directories)
            Scripts\   : jquery-1.10.2*.js/.map, jquery-migrate-1.2.1*.js,
                         jquery-ui-1.10.3.custom*.js, jquery.validate*.js,
                         jquery.validate.unobtrusive*.js, fineuploader   (12 files + 1 dir)
          Content\ionicons is STRUCTURALLY DIFFERENT between the two - the storefront has
          ionicons.css at the top level, the admin has css\ and fonts\ subdirectories - so
          whichever project published last would win, non-deterministically. Twelve of the
          Scripts\ collisions happen to be byte-identical today, which is exactly the kind
          of accident that makes this class of bug survive review.

      %(RecursiveDir) here is "Content/" or "Scripts/" - i.e. it ALREADY carries the prefix,
      because these are `Update` rules against items the SDK's project-rooted default glob
      created, not a fresh `Include="Content\**"`. Restating the prefix in the Link (the
      obvious first guess) publishes to Administration\Content\Content\... - MEASURED, and the
      audit caught it. Verified by evaluating the item metadata directly:
        Identity "Content/styles.css" -> RecursiveDir "Content/"
      and then by evaluating ResolvedFileToPublish: RelativePath goes from "Content/styles.css"
      to "Administration/Content/styles.css".

      NOTE this changes the PUBLISH path only. No CopyToOutputDirectory is set anywhere in
      this file, so the BUILD output is untouched and `dotnet run` of Nop.Web keeps serving
      these assets from the source tree at src\Presentation\Nop.Web\Administration\Content\
      - which is where they physically are, and where the two content-root-relative readers
      (RoxyFilemanController's conf.json and TinyMceHelper's langs\ probe) expect them.
    -->
    <None Update="Content\**"
          CopyToPublishDirectory="PreserveNewest"
          Link="Administration\%(RecursiveDir)%(Filename)%(Extension)" />
    <None Update="Scripts\**"
          CopyToPublishDirectory="PreserveNewest"
          Link="Administration\%(RecursiveDir)%(Filename)%(Extension)" />
    <None Update="db_backups\**"
          CopyToPublishDirectory="PreserveNewest"
